      "title": "One extra measurement halves qubit errors",
      "summary": "Researchers at the University of Regensburg and partners added a single measurement before a series of quantum operations. In their experiment this cut the error rate by more than half, which makes qubits more reliable without a redesign. It was a lab demonstration, and it still has to be shown to work on larger, more complex machines.",
